WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Thoracic Wall Musculature: Functional Anatomy of the Intercostal Spaces.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The intercostal spaces are occupied by three layers of muscle: external intercostal, internal intercostal, and innermost intercostal.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:01:10.000
The external intercostal fibers run obliquely inferomedially from the rib above to the rib below, elevating the ribs in inspiration.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:40.000
The internal intercostal fibers run inferolaterally, acting primarily during active or forced expiration.

00:01:40.000 --> 00:02:10.000
The intercostal neurovascular bundle runs in the costal groove along the lower border of each rib: Vein, Artery, Nerve (VAN from superior to inferior).

00:02:10.000 --> 00:02:28.000
Clinical Pearl: Chest tubes and thoracocentesis needles must be introduced strictly over the superior border of the lower rib to avoid VAN laceration.
